  "term": "triangulation",
  "definition": "In this historical psychology usage, triangulation means the mind’s act of placing an object in an independent position outside any one thought. James uses it for how, by noticing the same object across present and past thoughts, a person comes to regard it as a reality that can appear to multiple thoughts.",
